typhoon patch on fm1-base: advertising on or off (plat_ble_advertise), and the advertised name from fm1.toml
SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 (a change to fm1-base's MPL-2.0 files)

What: plat_ble_advertise(on) (include/plat.h): a computer may find and connect to the FM-1, or not; off lets a
connected computer go and keeps the device's link, so the FM-1 can be a central alone. ble/midi/le_midi.c keeps the
player's wish (adv_wanted) and set_adv_enable keeps to it, so none of the places that advertise again after a link
or a central's connection undoes it. fm1.toml ble_name = "..." (tools/build.py: 1..8 printable ASCII characters,
the advertising packet's room; checked there and in le_midi.c; FM1B_BLE_NAME, "FM-1" without it) is the name
advertised, with upstream's four hex digits of the FM-1's own after it in the scan response and the GAP name
("TYPHOON 1F2D": device/radio.c ble_midi_name); the start's log line says it, or "not advertising". ble_none.c and
the host simulator have it too (the host lets a connected computer go).
Why: typhoon's BLUETOOTH page, BLE-P (the FM-1 found by a computer) apart from BLE-C (the FM-1 connects to a device),
and the FM-1 shown in a computer's list as the firmware's name (TYPHOON).
Applies to: fm1-base 934e40d. After patches/fm1-base/0001 (the same files: host/plat_host.c, include/plat.h).
Upstream: not offered yet (charlesvestal/fm1-base).

